-- ind-c-tests-traces: independent tests (author ind-c) of the duties, powers and prohibitions, as #TRACE runs.
-- A DEONTIC value has no equality, so each expected outcome is an EXPECT comment directly ABOVE its #TRACE, read by check-traces.py
-- (the template in inputs/templates).  Time is the day number of `Day`; the trace starts on the day the rule's period runs from.
-- Row ids are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md; C-AFTER etc. are its counting conventions.

§ `ind-c duties with deadlines (Schedules 1 and 2)`

-- S1.1-03 (reading A): the notice on the latest day, 14 days before an appointment on 15 January 2026, is in time
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Sch 1 para 1(3) at least 2 weeks before appointing the Minister must present to the States a notice of intention` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2026 1 15) AT (Day (YMD 2025 12 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 1: the Minister presents a notice of intention to the States` AT (Day (YMD 2026 1 1))

-- S1.1-04: a notice 13 days before is late
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `Sch 1 para 1(3) at least 2 weeks before appointing the Minister must present to the States a notice of intention` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2026 1 15) AT (Day (YMD 2025 12 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 1: the Minister presents a notice of intention to the States` AT (Day (YMD 2026 1 2))

-- S1.1-02: the JAC's views never sought before the appointment
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `Sch 1 para 1(2) before appointing a person the Minister must seek the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2026 1 15) AT (Day (YMD 2025 12 1)) WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` (Day (YMD 2026 1 16)))

-- S1.3-08 (reading A): notice of a termination of 1 March 2026 on 15 March is in time; on 16 March late
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Sch 1 para 3(3) not more than 2 weeks after terminating the appointment the Minister must present to the States a notice that the Minister has terminated it` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2026 3 1) AT (Day (YMD 2026 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 1: the Minister presents a notice of the termination to the States` AT (Day (YMD 2026 3 15))

-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `Sch 1 para 3(3) not more than 2 weeks after terminating the appointment the Minister must present to the States a notice that the Minister has terminated it` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2026 3 1) AT (Day (YMD 2026 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 1: the Minister presents a notice of the termination to the States` AT (Day (YMD 2026 3 16))

-- S1.4-13 (reading A): the Commissioner's report for 2025 on 30 April 2026 is in time; on 1 May late
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Sch 1 para 4(9) the Commissioner must provide the Minister with the report as soon as practicable after the end of the year, and in no case later than 4 months after it` `the favoured interpretation` 2025 AT (Day (YMD 2025 12 31)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `Sch 1: the Commissioner provides the Minister with the report` AT (Day (YMD 2026 4 30))

-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Commissioner`
#TRACE `Sch 1 para 4(9) the Commissioner must provide the Minister with the report as soon as practicable after the end of the year, and in no case later than 4 months after it` `the favoured interpretation` 2025 AT (Day (YMD 2025 12 31)) WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `Sch 1: the Commissioner provides the Minister with the report` AT (Day (YMD 2026 5 1))

-- S1.4-18: a direction that requires the report to justify a decision about an individual charity
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `Sch 1 para 4(12) directions under sub-paragraph (11) must not require the report to contain justification of any decision of the Commissioner in relation to individual charities, governors or applicants for registration` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 1: the Minister directs that the report justify a decision` AT 5

-- S2.1-03: the 2 weeks' notice before appointing a tribunal member, a day late
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(3) at least 2 weeks before appointing a person as a tribunal member the Minister must present to the States a notice of intention` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2026 1 15) AT (Day (YMD 2025 12 1)) WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 2: the Minister presents a notice of intention to the States to appoint a member` AT (Day (YMD 2026 1 2))

-- S2.3-04: the responsible officer's report for 2025 on 1 May 2026 is late (reading A)
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the responsible officer of the tribunal under Schedule 2`
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 3(4) the responsible officer must provide the Minister with the report as soon as practicable after the end of the year, and in no case later than 4 months after it` `the favoured interpretation` 2025 AT (Day (YMD 2025 12 31)) WITH
    PARTY `the responsible officer of the tribunal under Schedule 2` DOES `Sch 2: the responsible officer provides the Minister with the report` AT (Day (YMD 2026 5 1))

-- S2.1-01: with 8 members, appointing a ninth is a breach
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `Sch 2 para 1(1) the Minister must not appoint more than 8 members of the tribunal` 8 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `Sch 2: the Minister appoints a person as a member of the tribunal` AT 3

§ `ind-c Articles 5 and 7`

-- A5-30: the Commissioner's duty to publish and maintain guidance is discharged by doing it
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 5(4) the Commissioner must publish and maintain guidance on the charity test` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `publish and maintain guidance` `the Commissioner` `the determination of whether an entity meets the charity test` AT 10

-- A7-05: the Commissioner presumes a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Commissioner`
#TRACE `Art 7(3)(a) the person determining must not presume a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit` `the Commissioner` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `presume a particular charitable purpose to be for the public benefit` `the Commissioner` AT 4

-- A7-06: 7(3) does not bind a governor
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 7(3)(a) the person determining must not presume a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit` `a governor` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a governor` DOES `presume a particular charitable purpose to be for the public benefit` `a governor` AT 4

§ `ind-c Articles 26, 29 and 30`

-- A26-36 with C-AFTER: a notice served 1 March 2026 requiring compliance within 14 days; compliance on 15 March is in time, none by 16 March is a breach
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 26(7) the person must comply with the requirement` `ind-c G8 A` (`a period of days fixed by the notice` 14) (YMD 2026 3 1) AT (Day (YMD 2026 3 1)) WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `comply with a requirement imposed under Article 26` AT (Day (YMD 2026 3 15))

-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `any person`
#TRACE `Art 26(7) the person must comply with the requirement` `ind-c G8 A` (`a period of days fixed by the notice` 14) (YMD 2026 3 1) AT (Day (YMD 2026 3 1)) WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` (Day (YMD 2026 3 16)))

-- A26-47: knowingly false information intended for an application
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `any person`
#TRACE `Art 26(10) the person must not give false information` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `provide information to the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE AT 2

-- A26-49: information not known to be false is not the prohibited act
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 26(10) the person must not give false information` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `provide information to the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE AT 2

-- A29-01: a disclosure to a journalist without consent
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `any person`
#TRACE `Art 29(1) the person must not disclose the information` `ind-c G8 A` FALSE (`Information received and its character` WITH `relates to the business or other affairs of a person` IS TRUE, `received under or for the purposes of this Law` IS TRUE, `received directly or indirectly from a person who so received it` IS FALSE, `already made available to the public from other sources` IS FALSE, `in the form of a summary or collection that identifies no particular person` IS FALSE) (`Disclosure of information` WITH `by or on behalf of the Commissioner` IS FALSE, `recipient` IS `a disclosure to any other person`, `to enable the Commissioner to discharge a function` IS FALSE, `to enable the recipient to discharge a function` IS FALSE, `to enable the recipient to discharge a function in relation to charities` IS FALSE, `for the investigation or prosecution of an offence` IS FALSE, `for taking or deciding whether to take proceedings under this Law` IS FALSE, `in circumstances prescribed by Regulations` IS FALSE, `required by the recipient for its functions` IS FALSE, `consent of the person to whom the information relates` IS FALSE, `consent of the person from whom the information was received` IS FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `disclose restricted information` AT 1

-- A30-01: the Commissioner discharges the duty to disclose to the Comptroller by disclosing
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 30(1) the Commissioner must disclose information to the Comptroller` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `disclose information to the Comptroller` AT 3

§ `ind-c whether a duty or power arises at all (a duty or power that arises and is unused stands; one that does not arise is FULFILLED)`

-- A26-33: a person who needs the retained document for business and has asked for it: the duty to supply a copy stands until performed
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 26(6) the Commissioner must supply a copy of the retained document` `ind-c G8 A` (`Request for a copy of a retained document` WITH `the person requires the document for the purpose of the person's business` IS TRUE, `the person has requested the document` IS TRUE, `day of the request` IS YMD 2026 5 1, `day the copy was supplied` IS NOTHING) NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- A26-34: asked, but no business need: no duty
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 26(6) the Commissioner must supply a copy of the retained document` `ind-c G8 A` (`Request for a copy of a retained document` WITH `the person requires the document for the purpose of the person's business` IS FALSE, `the person has requested the document` IS TRUE, `day of the request` IS YMD 2026 5 1, `day the copy was supplied` IS NOTHING) NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- A26-35: business need, never asked: no duty
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 26(6) the Commissioner must supply a copy of the retained document` `ind-c G8 A` (`Request for a copy of a retained document` WITH `the person requires the document for the purpose of the person's business` IS TRUE, `the person has requested the document` IS FALSE, `day of the request` IS YMD 2026 5 1, `day the copy was supplied` IS NOTHING) NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- A27-01: a ground, a relevant person, steps and a time specified: the permission to serve stands
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 27(2) the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice` (LIST `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`) `there has been misconduct by a registered charity` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- A27-11: no time specified for the steps: no power to serve such a notice
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 27(2) the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice` (LIST `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`) `there has been misconduct by a registered charity` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- A27-08: a former governor is not a relevant person: no power to serve on that person
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 27(2) the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice` (LIST `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct`) `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- A34-04: a vexatious appeal: the tribunal's power to award costs stands
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 34(3)(b) the tribunal may award costs` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- A34-06, A34-07: an appeal neither vexatious nor grossly unreasonable: no power to award costs
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 34(3)(b) the tribunal may award costs` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- A36-01: the Commissioner's power to reconsider stands whatever Part 8 says
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 36(1) the Commissioner may reconsider a decision` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- A6-32: the States' power to add a head stands on the Commissioner's recommendation
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 6(3) the States may add a sub-paragraph to Article 6(1) or (2)` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- A6-33: without the recommendation there is no power
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 6(3) the States may add a sub-paragraph to Article 6(1) or (2)` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- A30-01: required by the Comptroller, not yet disclosed: the duty stands
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 30(1) the Commissioner must disclose information to the Comptroller` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)

-- A30-07: not required: no duty
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 30(1) the Commissioner must disclose information to the Comptroller` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 10)
